  "summary": "A surface-wave magnitude 6.8 earthquake struck northern Armenia, then in the Soviet Union, on 7 December 1988, from slip on a thrust fault near Spitak. Between 25,000 and 50,000 people were killed. Poor construction drove the toll, and 113 countries sent aid in a sign of easing Cold War tensions.",
